  "worked_solution": "Writing the first few terms of the series explicitly, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{(n+1)!}{x}^{n+1}=2x-{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{4}+\u22ef.\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}^{\u2032}(x),$ we differentiate term-by-term. This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)=2-2x+{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\u22ef.\n$$",
